Not really
lacnuptruci'e
tumnoltruci'e

emphasize different aspects of feudalism.  You'd want to choose one that 
describes the society.  European feudalism focused on the power nobles 
acquired from land.  The chivalric concept of feudalism was a system of 
promise and reliance - service in exchange for protection.  Another 
version of feudalism would be based on the existence of serfdom 
(land-bound servants system?), which would certainly be important to 
Russian feudalism, but I don't know whether it applies to Oriental 
feudalism.

The important thing is to think about the concept you want to express 
and what Lojban words point towards that concept, turning to how it is 
expressed in other languages only to break down a mental block at coming 
up with an expression.

